```text
9. testing — 'all clear, proceed' gate
    test the backend in-process, no server, no browser, no real disk.
    seams already exist: DiskPort + ConfigParserPort are ABCs, so fake them.
    what to cover, in risk order:
      - ingestion / numap entity graph (validators, dep ordering, ingest regex)
      - kb state machine (handle_start, domain select, prompt select, hot path)
      - render pipeline (hydration, truncation, hot-prompt resolver, manifest)
      - apply_file_changes (block parsing, deletelist, fence stripping)
    shape:
      - one pytest file or small tests/ dir
      - fixture factories: in-memory disk (dict of path->content), fake cfg parser, canonical workspace
      - fake disk records writes/deletes for assertion
      - the gate is just: run pytest, exit 0 = green light
    out of scope:
      - http server wiring (thin delegation)
      - frontend (display layer)
      - gpu box proxy (pass-through)
```
```text
11. provider model:
    Clanker's system config can declare providers.
    The auth tokens and such would be carried in another file, contained in clanker repo but .gitignored. needs to be safe, anywayy

    a. commercial providers
       - anything that speaks /v1/chat/completions (this is openai's api?)
       - user supplies base_url + api_key (or no key for local)
       - this is the "default" shape, most providers fit here

    b. gpu-box (custom)
       - the tailnet-hosted thing, local GPU
       - adds host-side control: desktop/inference mode switching, raw box management

    c. noprovider public browser gui llm offerings on the free tier
       - basically the user will use the webui to get prompts to clipboard
       - paste those into webui of providers, converse
       - copy replies which are intented for ingestion over to clank webui, paste
```

